                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "354f7cb4-27d0-31d8-a7dd-419886b45bdb",
                                        "entry_id": "94dc7231-ba62-3bd7-87db-292fc52e1ee3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ridge or hill of sand piled up by currents of wind or water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25a225e4-516d-4160-a97f-a4e510a7c470",
                                                "sense_id": "354f7cb4-27d0-31d8-a7dd-419886b45bdb",
                                                "text": "Heavy line segments (lengthened for clarity) indicate locations of deep-sea dunes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d66e3728-dd2c-4930-9e8f-36dfb8c7847d",
                                                "sense_id": "354f7cb4-27d0-31d8-a7dd-419886b45bdb",
                                                "text": "In the early 2000s, space probes [confirmed Mars as] having dunes […] Their shapes are identical to their Saharan cousins', but they are ten times bigger. In contrast, underwater dunes are a hundred times smaller than their counterparts on solid ground. This universality of dunes is a blessing for physicists: their comparative study confirmed the models that describe the formation of dunes on Earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
